### Description

This Terraform program configures a Route 53 zone association between a VPC and a Route 53 zone. It includes the creation of a VPC and a Route 53 zone, and then associates the zone with the VPC using the `aws_route53_zone_association` resource. The program ensures that all required dependencies are met and follows the guidelines provided.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_vpc" "example_vpc" {
  cidr_block           = "10.0.0.0/16"
  enable_dns_support   = true
  enable_dns_hostnames = true
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "example_route53_zone" {
  name = "example.com"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone_association" "example_route53_zone_association" {
  vpc_id  = aws_vpc.example_vpc.id
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.example_route53_zone.zone_id
}
```

This configuration creates a VPC with a specified CIDR block and DNS settings, a Route 53 zone with a given domain name, and then associates the zone with the VPC. The `aws_route53_zone_association` resource ensures that the zone is correctly linked to the VPC.

