### Description
This Terraform program creates an Amazon Kendra index with user group resolution configuration. It includes an IAM role that is required by the Kendra index. The IAM role is configured with an assume role policy that allows it to be assumed by the Kendra service.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_role" {
  name = "kendra-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "kendra_index" {
  name       = "my-kendra-index"
  role_arn   = aws_iam_role.kendra_role.arn

  user_group_resolution_configuration {
    user_group_resolution_mode = "AWS_SSO"
  }
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.
2. **IAM Role**: An IAM role named `kendra-role` is created. The assume role policy allows the Kendra service to assume this role.
3. **Kendra Index**: A Kendra index named `my-kendra-index` is created. It references the IAM role created earlier and configures user group resolution using AWS Single Sign-On (SSO).

