LLM Output #0:
### Description
The Terraform program defines a DynamoDB table named `my_dynamodb_table` in the `us-west-2` region. The table uses on-demand capacity mode (`PAY_PER_REQUEST`) and includes the following attributes:
- `UserId` (hash key)
- `GameTitle` (range key)
- `TopScore`

Additionally, the table has TTL (Time To Live) enabled with the attribute `TimeToExist`. The table is tagged with `Name` and `Environment`.

### Terraform HCL Program
```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "my_dynamodb_table" {
  name           = "my_dynamodb_table"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "UserId"
  range_key      = "GameTitle"

  attribute {
    name = "UserId"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "GameTitle"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "TopScore"
    type = "N"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "TimeToExist"
    type = "N"
  }

  ttl {
    attribute_name = "TimeToExist"
    enabled        = true
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "my_dynamodb_table"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}
```

This configuration ensures that all attributes are indexed by including the `TimeToExist` attribute, which is required for TTL. The `billing_mode` is set to `PAY_PER_REQUEST` to enable on-demand capacity mode.

