### Description
The Terraform program defines an AWS SageMaker Pipeline resource along with an IAM role required for its execution. The SageMaker Pipeline includes a simple step that simulates a failure. The IAM role is configured with policies that provide full access to SageMaker and read-only access to S3.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_pipeline_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-pipeline-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  managed_policy_arns = [
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSageMakerFullAccess",
    "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess"
  ]
}

resource "aws_sagemaker_pipeline" "sagemaker_pipeline" {
  pipeline_name         = "my-sagemaker-pipeline"
  pipeline_display_name = "My-SageMaker-Pipeline"  # Fixed to valid characters
  role_arn              = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_pipeline_role.arn

  pipeline_definition = jsonencode({
    Version = "2020-12-01"
    Steps   = [
      {
        Name    = "TestStep"
        Type    = "Fail"
        Arguments = {
          ErrorMessage = "Test failure"
        }
      }
    ]
  })

  parallelism_configuration {
    max_parallel_execution_steps = 1
  }

  tags = {
    Environment = "Development"
  }
}
```

This configuration ensures that the `pipeline_display_name` uses only valid characters (a-z, A-Z, 0-9, and -), addressing the error reported by the Terraform plan. All other resources and configurations remain unchanged.

