To ensure that the provider has the necessary credentials, you can run the following command to configure the AWS CLI:

```sh
aws configure
```

This command will prompt you to enter your AWS Access Key ID, Secret Access Key, default region, and output format. Once you have configured the AWS CLI, Terraform will be able to authenticate with AWS and retrieve the necessary AMI information.

If you prefer not to use the AWS CLI, you can also set the `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` environment variables directly:

```sh
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="your_access_key_id"
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="your_secret_access_key"
```

After setting the environment variables, you can run `terraform init` and `terraform apply` to deploy the infrastructure.

