The Terraform program below creates a DynamoDB table with data encryption at rest enabled. The table is configured with a simple hash key and uses the default AWS KMS-managed key for encryption. The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "my_dynamodb_table" {
  name           = "my_dynamodb_table"
  billing_mode   = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
  hash_key       = "TestTableHashKey"

  attribute {
    name = "TestTableHashKey"
    type = "S"
  }

  server_side_encryption {
    enabled = true
  }
}
```

This configuration ensures that the DynamoDB table `my_dynamodb_table` is created with data encryption at rest enabled using the default AWS KMS-managed key. The table uses a simple hash key named `TestTableHashKey` of type `String`. The AWS provider is set to use the `us-west-2` region.

