This Terraform program creates a basic AWS IAM user named `basic_user` and attaches a basic SSH key to this user. The SSH key is specified in the `public_key` variable, which should be provided in either `ssh-rsa` or PEM format. The program ensures that the SSH key is correctly associated with the IAM user by using Terraform's resource dependencies.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "public_key" {
  description = "The SSH public key to attach to the IAM user."
  type        = string
  default     = "ssh-rsa  mytest@mydomain.com"
}

resource "aws_iam_user" "basic_user" {
  name = "basic_user"
}

resource "aws_iam_user_ssh_key" "basic_user_ssh_key" {
  username   = aws_iam_user.basic_user.name
  encoding   = "SSH"
  public_key = var.public_key
}
```

