1. Defines an AWS provider with the region set to `us-west-2`.
2. Creates an S3 bucket named `my-image-storage-bucket` with public read access.
3. Configures the S3 bucket as a website, setting `index.html` as the index document and `error.html` as the error document.
4. Uses the `aws_s3_bucket_website_configuration` resource to ensure the website configuration is applied correctly, referencing the S3 bucket created earlier.

