### Description of the Terraform Program

This Terraform program sets up a PostgreSQL 15 instance on AWS RDS within specific public subnets for running Airbyte connector test cases. The configuration includes the necessary parameters to ensure low maintenance and proper setup. The program uses the AWS provider and defines the required resources, including the RDS instance, security groups, and subnets.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

variable "db_subnet_group_name" {
  description = "Name of the DB subnet group"
  default     = "airbyte-subnet-group"
}

variable "db_instance_identifier" {
  description = "Identifier for the RDS instance"
  default     = "airbyte-postgres-instance"
}

variable "db_username" {
  description = "Username for the RDS instance"
  default     = "airbyteuser"
}

variable "db_password" {
  description = "Password for the RDS instance"
  default     = "securepassword123"
}

variable "public_subnet_ids" {
  description = "List of public subnet IDs"
  type        = list(string)
  default     = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]  # Replace with actual subnet IDs
}

resource "aws_db_subnet_group" "airbyte_subnet_group" {
  name       = var.db_subnet_group_name
  subnet_ids = var.public_subnet_ids

  tags = {
    Name = "AirbyteSubnetGroup"
  }
}

resource "aws_security_group" "airbyte_sg" {
  name        = "airbyte-security-group"
  description = "Security group for Airbyte PostgreSQL instance"
  vpc_id      = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with actual VPC ID

  ingress {
    from_port   = 5432
    to_port     = 5432
    protocol    = "tcp"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]  # Adjust as needed for security
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }

  tags = {
    Name = "AirbyteSecurityGroup"
  }
}

resource "aws_db_instance" "airbyte_postgres_instance" {
  identifier              = var.db_instance_identifier
  engine                  = "postgres"
  engine_version          = "15"
  instance_class          = "db.t3.medium"
  allocated_storage       = 500
  username                = var.db_username
  password                = var.db_password
  db_subnet_group_name    = aws_db_subnet_group.airbyte_subnet_group.name
  vpc_security_group_ids  = [aws_security_group.airbyte_sg.id]
  publicly_accessible     = true
  skip_final_snapshot     = true
  auto_minor_version_upgrade = true

  tags = {
    Name = "AirbytePostgresInstance"
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your desired region.

2. **Variables**: Several variables are defined to make the configuration flexible. Default values are provided for each variable.

3. **DB Subnet Group**: An `aws_db_subnet_group` resource is created to specify the subnets where the RDS instance will be deployed.

4. **Security Group**: An `aws_security_group` resource is created to allow inbound traffic on port 5432 (PostgreSQL default port) from any IP address (`0.0.0.0/0`). Adjust the `cidr_blocks` as needed for security.

5. **RDS Instance**: An `aws_db_instance` resource is created to set up the PostgreSQL 15 instance. The instance class is set to `db.t3.medium`, and the allocated storage is 500GB. The instance is made publicly accessible, and automatic minor version upgrades are enabled for low maintenance.

This configuration ensures that the PostgreSQL instance is properly set up for running Airbyte connector test cases within the specified public subnets.

