### Description

This Terraform program manages an AWS Lightsail Distribution with an S3 bucket as the origin. It includes the creation of a Lightsail bucket and a Lightsail distribution that references this bucket as its origin. The configuration ensures that the distribution is properly set up to serve content from the specified bucket.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_bucket" "lightsail_bucket_origin" {
  name      = "my-lightsail-bucket-origin"
  bundle_id = "small_1_0"
  force_delete = true
}

resource "aws_lightsail_distribution" "lightsail_distribution" {
  name      = "my-lightsail-distribution"
  bundle_id = "small_1_0"
  origin {
    name      = aws_lightsail_bucket.lightsail_bucket_origin.name
    region_name = "us-east-1"
  }
  default_cache_behavior {
    behavior = "cache"
  }
  cache_behavior_settings {
    allowed_http_methods = "GET,HEAD,OPTIONS,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE"
    cached_http_methods  = "GET,HEAD"
    default_ttl          = 86400
    maximum_ttl          = 31536000
    minimum_ttl          = 0
    forwarded_cookies {
      option = "none"
    }
    forwarded_headers {
      option = "default"
    }
    forwarded_query_strings {
      option = false
    }
  }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-east-1` region.
2. **Lightsail Bucket**: An `aws_lightsail_bucket` resource named `lightsail_bucket_origin` is created with a specified `bundle_id` and `force_delete` option enabled to ensure the bucket is deleted even if it contains objects.
3. **Lightsail Distribution**: An `aws_lightsail_distribution` resource named `lightsail_distribution` is created with the same `bundle_id`. It references the previously created bucket as its origin using the `origin` block. The `default_cache_behavior` and `cache_behavior_settings` blocks configure the caching behavior of the distribution.

