### Description

This Terraform program creates an Amazon S3 Glacier vault named `my_glacier_vault` and applies a Vault Lock policy to it. The Vault Lock policy is defined using an IAM policy document that denies deletion of archives older than 365 days. The `complete_lock` attribute is set to `false` initially, allowing for testing of the policy. To permanently apply the policy, you would need to change `complete_lock` to `true`.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault" "my_glacier_vault" {
  name = "my_glacier_vault"
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "example" {
  statement {
    actions = ["glacier:DeleteArchive"]
    effect  = "Deny"
    resources = [aws_glacier_vault.my_glacier_vault.arn]
    condition {
      test     = "NumericLessThanEquals"
      variable = "glacier:ArchiveAgeinDays"
      values   = ["365"]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_glacier_vault_lock" "my_glacier_vault_lock" {
  complete_lock = false  # Set to true to permanently apply the lock
  policy        = data.aws_iam_policy_document.example.json
  vault_name    = aws_glacier_vault.my_glacier_vault.name
}
```

### Notes

- Ensure that the Glacier Vault is empty before attempting to delete it.
- Set `complete_lock` to `true` to permanently apply the Vault Lock policy. Changing it to `false` is not possible once set to `true`.
- The region specified in the provider configuration (`us-west-2`) can be changed to any other valid AWS region as per your requirement.

